[{:db/id 17592186278344 :question/problem "![](images/36/3621e70552c3891f43521e74704d5db3f276f9928669390d688cca1bc3449217.png)\n\nConsider the rectangular region $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane, given by\n\n$$\nΔ=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,1\\le u\\le \\sqrt{3},\\,\\,\\frac{6\\pi }{5}\\le v\\le \\frac{4\\pi }{3}\\},\n$$\n\nand the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v).\n$$\n\nFind the image of $Δ$ under the action of $T.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198375 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-57a07fec-924e-51b2-9054-16b08d5b6be1"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-57a07fec-924e-51b2-9054-16b08d5b6be1" :question/id #uuid "57a07fec-924e-51b2-9054-16b08d5b6be1" :question/math-academy-id "q-160949" :question/problem "![](images/6b/6b0365b0f6b00859fb3739876f7d9a119db8b7f649e1935c66091285460e7f70.png)\n\nConsider the region $D$ in the $xy$-plane, shown above. The transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (x(u,v),\\,y(u,v)),\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nx=u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,y=u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\n$$\n\nmaps the region $Δ$ from the $uv$-plane to $D.$ Which of the following could be the region $Δ?$" :question/worked-solution "For our transformation $T,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,y=u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v.\n$$\n\nNotice that if we change $u$ to $r$ and $v$ to $\\theta ,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich represents the usual formulas for changing from polar to Cartesian coordinates. \n\nTherefore, the pre-image $Δ$ of $D$ under the action of $T$ is the region that can be written as \n\n$$\nΔ=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\le v\\le \\frac{\\pi }{4}\\}.\n$$\n\nThis is the rectangular region enclosed between\n\n- two vertical lines with Cartesian equations $u=0$ and $u=1,$ and\n\n- two horizontal lines with Cartesian equations $v=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ and $v=\\frac{\\pi }{4},$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/40/40d60714c368f92bd7382005882c627be119f6cb05665441730887b60306cdb7.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e1fe8e38-4aad-57a4-8a8d-5a0d162037eb"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e1fe8e38-4aad-57a4-8a8d-5a0d162037eb" :answer-field/id #uuid "e1fe8e38-4aad-57a4-8a8d-5a0d162037eb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-8c755e5e-6783-571f-a88c-164c24a1dfcd" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8c755e5e-6783-571f-a88c-164c24a1dfcd" "answer-da76ff9a-9c3b-5dcc-86dd-ebe90f5c27fb" "answer-98deceaf-7a7c-5395-80de-66909b2600ae" "answer-87b9e5b4-dff5-5eec-ba80-fedc99f32b46" "answer-f1bfc4f2-05c7-5141-aec8-57ca2deb933f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8c755e5e-6783-571f-a88c-164c24a1dfcd" :answer/id #uuid "8c755e5e-6783-571f-a88c-164c24a1dfcd" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/40/40d60714c368f92bd7382005882c627be119f6cb05665441730887b60306cdb7.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-da76ff9a-9c3b-5dcc-86dd-ebe90f5c27fb" :answer/id #uuid "da76ff9a-9c3b-5dcc-86dd-ebe90f5c27fb" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/71/716d1dc2aee5a523e5a9619fdf166f2a9fccd02475212752baea44a26a9db47f.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-98deceaf-7a7c-5395-80de-66909b2600ae" :answer/id #uuid "98deceaf-7a7c-5395-80de-66909b2600ae" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/f0/f0419b0c1195c443579bc12cf5ab8abd4b0d115ddb6f9ac24f9cf367fb82c2b6.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-87b9e5b4-dff5-5eec-ba80-fedc99f32b46" :answer/id #uuid "87b9e5b4-dff5-5eec-ba80-fedc99f32b46" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/f3/f3425325c560606e15fc752f18e637f7ccab0eec8c973f022a4976b8477a7492.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f1bfc4f2-05c7-5141-aec8-57ca2deb933f" :answer/id #uuid "f1bfc4f2-05c7-5141-aec8-57ca2deb933f" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/fe/fee321af3b544d653c22ff2c7a573dd1c8cd3c93bf42bd65d592f7264a49de74.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198384 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-6caf644a-b965-5b35-b048-eee4060c43c4"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186278351 :question/problem "![](images/70/708bf4df2d45383b0dd367f5bfe3dc9e260a17cfefe0566e2b6d37dec98af2ef.png)\n\nConsider the square region $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane, given by\n\n$$\nΔ=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 3,\\,\\,\\frac{5\\pi }{9}\\le v\\le \\frac{5\\pi }{6}\\},\n$$\n\nand the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v).\n$$\n\nWhich of the following could be the image of the top side of $Δ$ under the action of $T?$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-6caf644a-b965-5b35-b048-eee4060c43c4" :question/id #uuid "6caf644a-b965-5b35-b048-eee4060c43c4" :question/math-academy-id "q-161034" :question/problem "![](images/b3/b3bef2dbb84cfe3a2881abf8f61761f98ea0d9cf4a07ea582355c57d375f975d.png)\n\nConsider the square region $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane, given by\n\n$$\nΔ=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,3\\le u\\le 6,\\,\\,\\frac{3\\pi }{2}\\le v\\le \\frac{7\\pi }{4}\\},\n$$\n\nand the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v).\n$$\n\nThe image of the top side of $Δ$ under the action of $T$ is a line segment. Which of the following statements are true regarding the image?\n\nI. The image makes the angle of $\\frac{3\\pi }{2}$ with the positive $x$-axis.\n\nII. The image makes the angle of $\\frac{7\\pi }{4}$ with the positive $x$-axis.\n\nIII. The endpoints of the image lie on the circles of radii $3$ and $6$ centered at $O.$" :question/worked-solution "To map the entire region $Δ$ onto the $xy$-plane, we consider the transformation of each side. However, in this case, we consider only the top side.\n\nFor the top side, we have $v=\\frac{7\\pi }{4}$ and $3\\le u\\le 6.$ \n\nSubstituting $v=\\frac{7\\pi }{4}$ into our transformation equations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x,y) & =T(u,v) \\\\  & =(u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v) \\\\  & =(u\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{4}),\\,u\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{4})),\\,3\\le u\\le 6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is a parametric equation of the line segment shown below.\n\n![](images/b9/b976e62862ba82dfd89ff28627239dd5b5d1be1144e257223c091f29a5729f89.png)\n\n \n\nNote that the line that this segment lies on passes through the origin. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is false, while statement II is true. The slope of the line is\n\n$$\nk=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{4})}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{4})}=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{4}).\n$$\n\nAs a result, our line makes an angle of $\\frac{7\\pi }{4}$ radians with the positive $x$-axis.\n\n- Statement III is true.\n\n- When $u=3,$ we obtain the point \n$(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{4}),\\,3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{4})),$\nwhose distance to the origin is $3.$\n\n- When $u=6,$ we obtain the point \n$(6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{4}),\\,6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{4})),$\nwhose distance to the origin is $6.$\n\nSo, the endpoints of the line segment lie on the circles of radii $3$ and $6.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8cd74140-69a0-5af3-8672-f40c3db56533"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8cd74140-69a0-5af3-8672-f40c3db56533" :answer-field/id #uuid "8cd74140-69a0-5af3-8672-f40c3db56533" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-de7d22b9-d57c-5d7b-88cb-f0b4ca5f4a5d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9d738677-4b48-5272-ba62-6f070fe8babb" "answer-d5079a63-2c21-5532-8a24-134a5b4af955" "answer-de7d22b9-d57c-5d7b-88cb-f0b4ca5f4a5d" "answer-a8188bf8-8b54-575b-933a-aa859ce24d7c" "answer-3d20667f-50b2-55b0-95fa-20f52b560b36"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9d738677-4b48-5272-ba62-6f070fe8babb" :answer/id #uuid "9d738677-4b48-5272-ba62-6f070fe8babb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d5079a63-2c21-5532-8a24-134a5b4af955" :answer/id #uuid "d5079a63-2c21-5532-8a24-134a5b4af955" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-de7d22b9-d57c-5d7b-88cb-f0b4ca5f4a5d" :answer/id #uuid "de7d22b9-d57c-5d7b-88cb-f0b4ca5f4a5d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a8188bf8-8b54-575b-933a-aa859ce24d7c" :answer/id #uuid "a8188bf8-8b54-575b-933a-aa859ce24d7c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3d20667f-50b2-55b0-95fa-20f52b560b36" :answer/id #uuid "3d20667f-50b2-55b0-95fa-20f52b560b36" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None of the statements are true" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186389153 :question/worked-solution "For our transformation $T,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,y=u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v.\n$$\n\nNotice that if we change $u$ to $r$ and $v$ to $\\theta ,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich represents the usual formulas for changing from polar to Cartesian coordinates. \n\nTherefore, the pre-image $Δ$ of $D$ under the action of $T$ is the region that can be written as \n\n$$\nΔ=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,1\\le u\\le 2,\\,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le v\\le \\frac{5\\pi }{4}\\}.\n$$\n\nThis is the rectangular region enclosed between\n\n- two vertical lines with Cartesian equations $u=1$ and $u=2,$ and\n\n- two horizontal lines with Cartesian equations $v=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and $v=\\frac{5\\pi }{4},$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/88/88d58291666ed60113e3d16c5bc30e6d4375cbae3501f8e3e26bd9bbacb4940d.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "activity-5c82b827-3e4e-5f9f-9368-26da9d8bf53c" :activity/id #uuid "5c82b827-3e4e-5f9f-9368-26da9d8bf53c" :activity/title "Polar Coordinate Transformations" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186049321 :activity/course 17592186046659 :activity/steps ["step-64d08072-1a49-5e0c-9af1-0ecfb9d8073a" "step-d73744fd-8d46-5808-92e1-0ec7ee597069" "step-3e559c32-32ad-5b51-a713-cef4abf5f5ca" "step-9b9a8694-189b-58cf-bf5d-4a0e9eed87f4" "step-d7f0238c-5d88-53fd-9153-3c953fcbb734"] :activity/first-step "step-64d08072-1a49-5e0c-9af1-0ecfb9d8073a" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-64d08072-1a49-5e0c-9af1-0ecfb9d8073a" :step/id #uuid "64d08072-1a49-5e0c-9af1-0ecfb9d8073a" :step/content 17592186278344 :step/next "step-d73744fd-8d46-5808-92e1-0ec7ee597069" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-d73744fd-8d46-5808-92e1-0ec7ee597069" :step/id #uuid "d73744fd-8d46-5808-92e1-0ec7ee597069" :step/content "question-57a07fec-924e-51b2-9054-16b08d5b6be1" :step/next "step-3e559c32-32ad-5b51-a713-cef4abf5f5ca" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-3e559c32-32ad-5b51-a713-cef4abf5f5ca" :step/id #uuid "3e559c32-32ad-5b51-a713-cef4abf5f5ca" :step/content 17592186278351 :step/next "step-9b9a8694-189b-58cf-bf5d-4a0e9eed87f4" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-9b9a8694-189b-58cf-bf5d-4a0e9eed87f4" :step/id #uuid "9b9a8694-189b-58cf-bf5d-4a0e9eed87f4" :step/content "question-6caf644a-b965-5b35-b048-eee4060c43c4" :step/next "step-d7f0238c-5d88-53fd-9153-3c953fcbb734" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-d7f0238c-5d88-53fd-9153-3c953fcbb734" :step/id #uuid "d7f0238c-5d88-53fd-9153-3c953fcbb734" :step/content 17592186389153 :db/ensure [:step/validate]}]
